up, it was beautiful, and I decided to turn around. I went back, I was cold, just kind of damp. I went right to our kitchen, I pulled a sheet of paper out and said, Vic, you have to help yourself. And I don't know how to explain this either, Vic, you have to help yourself. And I don't know how to explain this either, but it was almost as if I was looking down on myself from the ceiling and just looking at my head, looking at the piece of paper and pen and saying, what are you going to do to help yourself, Vic? Almost like I was my own therapist.

